kosha stone

  -- generic term for naturally occurring hard mineral aggregates.
  -- granite: interlocked crystals of quartz + feldspar + mica.
  -- limestone: CaCO3 — sedimentary. marble: metamorphic limestone.
  -- sandstone: SiO2 grains cemented by silica or calcite.
  -- basalt: volcanic. fine-grained. dense.
  --
  -- properties:
  --   very hard (7+ Mohs for granite, quartz)
  --   brittle — fractures without plastic deformation
  --   high compressive strength, low tensile strength (like concrete)
  --   coefficient of restitution: ~0.2-0.4
  --   thermal insulator at everyday scale (k ≈ 2-4 W/mK)
  --   high density (granite ≈ 2700 kg/m³)
  --   chemically stable (except limestone in acid)

